From: Captain-Tripps
Subject: [PATCH] sycl prefill: grouped expert path for IQ3_S, both cards, ESIMD GEMM option

Three changes to the prompt-read expert path (STRATA_NIGHT_PREFILL_GROUPED).

1. Per-layer type check. The grouped path was all-or-nothing on the
   model's expert types, so a quant mix with one unsupported layer (IQ3_S:
   one IQ4_XS layer, some Q2_0 down layers) never took it. Each layer now
   checks its own types (night_grouped_layer_ok) and falls back to dequant
   + oneMKL on its own. Chunks shorter than STRATA_NIGHT_PREFILL_GROUPED_MIN_T
   (default 256) also keep the old path, so MTP verify windows are unchanged.

2. The second card. peer_alias_resident required m.T_max == 12288 and a
   whole-model type list, so at --prefill 8192 the expert-parallel card
   never ran the grouped path. The rows buffer is T_max*K*N*4, so the pin
   is not needed; it is now m.T_max > 0, and the type check is per layer.
   stderr prints "peer alias path on/off (T_max N)" once.

3. STRATA_NIGHT_PREFILL_ESIMD=1 runs the grouped experts' GEMMs on the
   llama.cpp SYCL fork's ESIMD grouped dequant GEMM (llama.cpp#31428 plus
   an IQ2_S loader and 64-wide tiles), linked through a small C shim
   (strata_esimd_shim.cpp) built as its own object library, because the
   fork's dpct helper and Strata's dpct headers both define namespace dpct.
   Gate/up run as one stacked GEMM when the up rows follow the gate rows,
   then a split-layout SwiGLU, then down. Types the kernel does not cover
   (Q2_0 down) fall back to night_grouped_f16. CMake builds it only when
   STRATA_ESIMD_DIR and STRATA_ESIMD_FORK are set. Entry lists go up
   through a small pinned ring (STRATA_NIGHT_PREFILL_PINNED_UP, default 1).
   With STRATA_PREFILL_TIMING the peer timeline adds grouped prep, grouped
   gate/up, grouped act+down and reduce.

Measured (Windows, 2x Arc Pro B70, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GSQ-RCO IQ3_S,
--prefill 8192, timing off, 32k-token prompt, three interleaved rounds):
base 1,680 tok/s, (1) 1,989, (1)+(3) on card 0 2,132, all three 2,194
(+31%). Decode unchanged (114-116 short, 106-108 after 32k). Greedy
output: first tokens identical at 32k; an 8k answer rewords at token 4
(rounding-level drift, same content).

---
diff --git a/sycl/CMakeLists.txt b/sycl/CMakeLists.txt
index 56becbb..cd64fb4 100644
--- a/sycl/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/sycl/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -280,6 +280,22 @@ target_compile_options(strata_prefill PUBLIC ${_strata_mkl})
 target_link_options(strata_prefill PUBLIC ${_strata_mkl})
 target_link_libraries(strata_prefill PUBLIC strata_engine)
 
+# night lab: the llama.cpp SYCL fork's ESIMD grouped dequant GEMM for the grouped prefill experts
+# (STRATA_NIGHT_PREFILL_ESIMD). Off unless STRATA_ESIMD_DIR (fused-gemm-esimd.cpp + strata_esimd_shim.cpp) and
+# STRATA_ESIMD_FORK (the fork's ggml dir) are set; built with the fork's headers, apart from Strata's dpct.
+set(STRATA_ESIMD_DIR "" CACHE PATH "dir with fused-gemm-esimd.cpp and strata_esimd_shim.cpp")
+set(STRATA_ESIMD_FORK "" CACHE PATH "the llama.cpp SYCL fork's ggml dir")
+if(STRATA_ESIMD_DIR AND STRATA_ESIMD_FORK)
+  add_library(strata_esimd OBJECT ${STRATA_ESIMD_DIR}/fused-gemm-esimd.cpp ${STRATA_ESIMD_DIR}/strata_esimd_shim.cpp)
+  target_include_directories(strata_esimd BEFORE PRIVATE ${STRATA_ESIMD_DIR} ${STRATA_ESIMD_FORK}/src/ggml-sycl
+                             ${STRATA_ESIMD_FORK}/src ${STRATA_ESIMD_FORK}/include)
+  target_compile_definitions(strata_esimd PRIVATE GGML_SYCL_F16 GGML_SYCL_SUPPORT_XMX GGML_SYCL_WARP_SIZE=16
+                             GGML_SYCL_XMX_AOT_SG=16 MKL_ILP64 NOMINMAX _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS)
+  target_compile_options(strata_esimd PRIVATE -Wno-narrowing)
+  target_sources(strata_prefill PRIVATE $<TARGET_OBJECTS:strata_esimd>)
+  target_compile_definitions(strata_prefill PRIVATE STRATA_ESIMD=1)
+endif()
+
 strata_resolve(_main src/program/generate.cpp)
 add_executable(strata ${_main})
 target_link_libraries(strata PRIVATE strata_engine strata_prefill strata_spec)
